  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $h(n)$ be minimal such that any group $G$ with the property that any subset of $>n$ elements contains some $x\neq y$ such that $xy=yx$ can be covered by at most $h(n)$ many Abelian subgroups.\nEstimate $h(n)$ as well as possible.",
